<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Default Debug entitlements for the AnglesiteRemote login-item helper (#1208 P2).
         Identical to Resources/AnglesiteRemote.entitlements minus keychain-access-groups.

         Why this file exists, mirroring Resources/Anglesite-Debug.entitlements' role for the main
         app: keychain-access-groups requires Apple to issue a real provisioning profile even under
         Manual/ad-hoc code signing, and Xcode refuses to build the target at all once it is
         present without a Team —

             error: "AnglesiteRemote" requires a provisioning profile. Enable development signing
             and select a provisioning profile in the Signing & Capabilities editor.

         That is the same class of blocker #1038 documents for the iCloud entitlement, and #1204
         for Associated Domains. It is NOT the Apple Developer portal kind: Keychain Sharing needs
         no portal capability, every App ID carries it implicitly. Only signing is gated.

         README.md / CONTRIBUTING.md promise a clone-and-build with no Apple Developer account, so
         this CI-safe file must stay free of any Team-requiring capability. Selected via
         $(ANGLESITE_REMOTE_DEBUG_ENTITLEMENTS) in xcconfig/Signing-Debug.xcconfig.

         Consequence at runtime, deliberate and loud rather than silent: a Debug build signed
         against this file cannot open the shared pairing keychain item, so
         DevicePairingSettingsView.generateQRCode() reports "couldn't prepare pairing key" instead
         of rendering a QR, and anglesite-remote-helper's helperSigningKey() falls back to an
         ephemeral key with a warning. A contributor with a real Team who wants the real behavior
         locally opts into Resources/AnglesiteRemote-Debug-Keychain.entitlements (and, on the main
         app side, Resources/Anglesite-Debug-iCloud.entitlements) from a gitignored
         xcconfig/Signing-Debug.local.xcconfig — see Signing-Debug.local.xcconfig.example. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- Bridges P2P channels to the container's loopback proxies, and (eventually) accepts
         inbound WebRTC ICE hole-punch traffic — see design spec §2 "no standing listening ports"
         (ICE binds ephemeral ports; that's not a stable inbound service). -->
    <key>com.apple.security.network.server</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- Own bookmark store for non-iCloud sites (design spec §2 "File access") — the main app's
         bookmarks are app-scoped and don't transfer to this bundle ID. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.files.bookmarks.app-scope</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- Apple Containerization framework (#69): boot local OCI containers, same as Anglesite.app. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.virtualization</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
